#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0047 expect=violation domain=ADAE
#note "PLAN-occds-source-domain-by-ig D1/D2, on OUR metadata store: ADAE under the D10-inferred OCCDS 1.0 (base Req STUDYID, USUBJID, --SEQ, --TERM, CMTRT, AESER) with NO AESEQ column. The source domain comes from the occurrence variables the dataset carries (ADaMIG-OCCDS 1.1 §3: the 2-letter prefix of the variable name is the SDTM domain), never from its name: AETERM / AEDECOD name AE, so --SEQ / --TERM resolve to AESEQ / AETERM and are demanded, and the absent AESEQ is reported; CMTRT carries the CM prefix and the dataset gives evidence of AE only, so it is not demanded; AESER (AE) is, and is absent -> one violation naming [AESEQ, AESER]. Under round-2 R2-1 (domain from the AD<dd> name, confirmed by <dd>SEQ) the missing AESEQ confirmed no domain, --SEQ was not demanded, and only [AESER] was reported."
#library-ref standard=adamig version=1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt "$missing_required_variables"="[AESEQ, AESER]"
dataset ADAE
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col AETERM type=Char label="Reported Term for the Adverse Event"
col AEDECOD type=Char label="Dictionary-Derived Term"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | HEADACHE | HEADACHE
---
